# monarch keeps ONLY these firmware files (in /usr/lib/firmware). Every other
# firmware file is deleted after firmware or kernel installs and updates by
# /usr/local/sbin/monarch-trim-hardware (pacman hook 70-monarch-trim-hardware).
# Patterns are shell patterns; * also matches across folders.
#
# Add firmware: add a line, then reinstall its package, e.g.
#   sudo pacman -S linux-firmware-intel
# Keep ALL firmware: put a line with only * , then reinstall the firmware packages.
# See /usr/share/monarch/HARDWARE.md.

# --- ThinkPad L14 Gen 5 (21L2), Intel Core Ultra 5 135U (Meteor Lake) ---
# Graphics: Meteor Lake (i915): display (DMC), GuC, HuC, GSC
i915/mtl_*
# Wi-Fi: Intel AX211 (Meteor Lake CNVi, chip "ma-b0-gf-a0")
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-ma-b0-gf-a0*
# Bluetooth: Intel AX211
intel/ibt-0180-0041.*
# NVIDIA driver (monarch-add-nvidia, only installed when chosen)
nvidia/*
# Sound: Sound Open Firmware for Meteor Lake, and its generic topology
intel/sof-ipc4/mtl/*
intel/sof-ipc4-lib/mtl/*
intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-hda-generic*
# CPU fixes (microcode): family 6, model 0xAA, stepping 4
intel-ucode/06-aa-04*
# Wi-Fi radio rules per country
regulatory.db*
